          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On Saturday, November 29, 2014, around 11:15 PM, an individual was intrigued by the swift and silent passage of a bright, orange-yellow light shape in the sky. The phenomenon moved along a straight trajectory. No other testimonies were collected. The passage of an orange glowing ball on a Saturday evening evokes a Thai lantern, likely released nearby after a private party. The witness looked towards south-southwest, the object moved from his left to his right as it distanced itself. The wind in Le Mans was northeast (see Météociel report). This wind is consistent with the direction taken by the glowing object. The GEIPAN GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
